COMPSTAT(1)                 User Commands                COMPSTAT(1)

NAME
    compstat - print or reset the frame statistics of X12

SYNOPSIS
    compstat [-r] [-p]

DESCRIPTION
    compstat reads the frame statistics of the display server X12
    through the debug interface and prints them on one line as
    key=value pairs. The statistics cover the period since the start
    of X12 or since the last reset. Times are microseconds.

    frames, rects, pixels
        compositions, composed damage rectangles and composed device
        pixels
    flushes, flush_bytes
        flushes of the framebuffer and the bytes they copied
    compose_us, compose_max_us, flush_us, flush_max_us
        the time spent composing and flushing, in total and for the
        slowest frame
    frame_max_us, frame_p50_us, frame_p95_us, frame_p99_us
        the longest frame and the frame time below which 50, 95 and
        99 percent of the frames lie
    damage_latency_us, commit_latency_us, input_latency_us
        the average time from the first damage, from the earliest
        commit of a buffer and from the earliest pointer motion to the
        end of the frame that shows it, each also as a _max_us value
    wakeups, idle_timers
        returns of the main loop and frame timer expirations without
        damage
    cpu_us
        the CPU time of X12, with a resolution of one millisecond
    back_bytes, pool_bytes
        the bytes of the back buffer and of the mapped client buffers
    cursor_moves, cursor_us
        moves of the device cursor and the time they took. On a
        device with a hardware cursor, a pointer motion moves that
        cursor and composes no frame. The end of the move then ends
        the input latency.

OPTIONS
    -r    reset the statistics instead of printing them
    -p    with -r, print the statistics before the reset

EXAMPLES
    compstat
    compstat -r -p
